<h2>Where should the filters sit on the activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only. Controls shown are the likely set (Event select, date range, search); which filters to include is a separate question.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="inline" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A. Inline filter row above the table</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p><strong>Account activity</strong></p>
          <p class="label">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin:8px 0">
            <div><div class="label">Event</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" style="width:130px"></div>
            <div><div class="label">From</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sep 14, 2026" style="width:100px"></div>
            <div><div class="label">To</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sep 28, 2026" style="width:100px"></div>
            <div><div class="label">Search</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Device, location, IP" style="width:150px"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="label">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>Inline row</h3>
      <p>Always visible, one glance to see what is filtered. Wraps to stacked fields at 320px. Least JS.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="panel" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B. Filter panel beside the table</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p><strong>Account activity</strong></p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:16px">
            <div class="mock-sidebar" style="min-width:140px">
              <div class="label">Event</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" style="width:120px">
              <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">From</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sep 14, 2026" style="width:120px">
              <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">To</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sep 28, 2026" style="width:120px">
              <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">Search</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Device, location" style="width:120px">
            </div>
            <div style="flex:1">
              <p class="label">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
              <div class="placeholder">Table (narrower)</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>Side panel</h3>
      <p>Room for more filters later, but takes width from a six-column table and needs its own reflow rules.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="popover" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C. Filter button with popover and tags</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p><strong>Account activity</strong></p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
            <span class="label">[Sign-in failed x]</span>
            <span class="label">[Last 7 days x]</span>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px dashed currentColor;padding:8px;width:200px;margin-bottom:8px">
            <div class="label">Popover (open)</div>
            <div class="label">Event / From / To / Search</div>
          </div>
          <p class="label">Showing 3 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table (full width)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>Popover + removable tags</h3>
      <p>Compact, active filters shown as tags. One more click to reach the controls; most JS and focus handling.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
